  "recipe": {
    "technique": "7 m (6 to 12 ft) in height. The production is closely controlled and limited in number to maintain quality. While the primary production is of Hindu deities, artisans also cast animal figures, portraits and other motifs based on requirements. Casting is done using the ancient lost-wax process (cire perdue), producting either solid or hollow casts. For solid castings, artisans prepare an original model form a wax compund made of pure beeswax, tree resin (kungiliyam), and groundnut oil in a 4:4:1 ratio."
  },
